        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=MO003"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town of Moffett was named for Martha Moffett Payne, the wife of a prominent local resident.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moffett%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moffett developed into an agricultural center for cotton farmers and established a post office in 1908.",
